+``--sub-video-rect-aspect=<no|ratio>``
+    Place subtitles against the largest centered rectangle of the given aspect
+    ratio inside the displayed video rectangle, instead of against the video
+    rectangle itself (default: no). Zero is identical to ``no``.
+
+    This is for a user shader that composites the true picture, centered and
+    at its own aspect ratio, inside a frame whose aspect ratio was changed with
+    ``--video-aspect-override`` (for example to fill the window with a blurred
+    ambient border). Without it, subtitles and image subtitles follow the
+    overridden frame: ASS events anchored to a corner land in the corner of the
+    window rather than the corner of the picture.
+
+    Text subtitles still may use the space outside this rectangle, depending on
+    ``--sub-use-margins`` and similar options.
+
